    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383-a1">

                <pb facs="0523" n="265" xml:id="pg265"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 155630/15]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 28, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: With reference to the note
                    which your excellency was good enough to address to me on the 18th ultimo
                    respecting the shipment to the Mitchell-Bissell Company of New York of 153
                    cases, of German porcelain guides, I have the honour to inform your excellency,
                    that after due consideration of the case, His Majesty’s Government have decided
                    to raise no objection to the passage of these goods, and His Majesty’s Consul
                    General at Rotterdam is being instructed to issue, on application, a permit for
                    their shipment.</p>
                <p>I would, however, observe that these goods could well be supplied from this
                    country, and it is only because the delay required to place the orders might
                    prove inconvenient for the users in the United States of America that His
                    Majesty’s Government have decided to treat the present application as a special
                    case. The grant of a permit for the whole amount in this instance must there
                    fore not be considered in any way as a precedent for dealing with future
                    applications of this kind.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
